  "title": "Let's make plans",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Making plans together.**\n\n- 'Let's…' = **চল / চলো / চলেন** + the আমি present: **চলো, বেড়াতে যাই** 'Let's go out'.\n- Invite with a future question: **তুমি কি আমাদের সাথে যাবে?** 'Will you come with us?' To an elder: **আপনি কি … আসবেন?**\n- Purpose with **-তে**: **ছবি দেখতে যাব** 'I'll go to see a film', **খেতে যাই** 'let's go and eat'.\n\nAccept with **অবশ্যই আসব** 'Of course I'll come'. No আমি needed: -ব already says 'I'.\n\nMuslim speakers often add **ইনশাআল্লাহ** 'God willing' to a plan: **ইনশাআল্লাহ, আমি আসব।** Hindu speakers don't use it; a plain future is fine for everyone.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "inshaallah",
      "bn": "ইনশাআল্লাহ",
      "tr": "inshaallah",
      "en": "God willing",
      "notes": "Muslim speakers add it to plans: ইনশাআল্লাহ, আমি আসব. Also written ইনশাল্লাহ. Hindu speakers don't use it."
    },
    {
      "id": "berate",
      "bn": "বেড়াতে",
      "tr": "berate",
      "en": "to go out (on a visit or trip)",
      "notes": "With যাওয়া: বেড়াতে যাব 'I'll go out / go on a trip / go visiting'."
    },
    {
      "id": "dekhte",
      "bn": "দেখতে",
      "tr": "dekhte",
      "en": "to see",
      "notes": "-তে + a verb of motion gives purpose: ছবি দেখতে যাব 'I'll go to see a film'."
    }
  ],
